        <mxCell id="n5" value="&lt;b&gt;⚠ Scale note&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The paper's β particles are ~22.8 nm, larger than the ~7.4 nm grains in this 20 nm box, so the precipitate edge is scaled down to 3.5 nm. The Burgers OR, GB-only nucleation, block morphology and ~10 vol% are kept.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a geometric construction of the final microstructure, not a nucleation/kinetics simulation; the interfaces still need relaxing in LAMMPS afterwards." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;dashed=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1030" y="1025" width="270" height="200" as="geometry" />
